  "final_text": "I can't name the cheapest offer yet. Offers B and C don't include delivery, and the files don't give a freight or storage cost for them. Once freight and storage are added, any of the three could come out cheapest. Here's the comparison for 40,000 boxes a year (from `anfrage.md:16`), delivered to Brandtwerk, Nordhessen:\n\n| Line | A Nürnberg | B Poznań | C Brno | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Unit price | €0.66 | €0.52 (€520 per 1,000) | €0.575 (€57.50 per 100) | A:16, B:13, C:15 |\n| Goods (40,000 pcs) | €26,400 | €20,800 | €23,000 | calculated |\n| Freight | €0 (supplier delivers to your plant, DAP) | **missing**: you collect from Poznań (EXW) | **missing**: you collect from Brno (FCA) | A:21, B:16, C:18 |\n| One-off | €0 | €1,450 die-cutting tool | €0 | A:19, B:21, C:11 |\n| Storage | small orders (min. 3,000 pcs) | **missing**: min. 20,000 pcs per order | **missing**: 10,000 pcs per delivery | A:22, B:14, C:17 |\n| Early-payment discount (if you take it) | −€528 (2%) | −€416 (2%, goods only, not the tool) | −€690 (3%) | A:24, B:17+22, C:19 |\n| **Total** | **€25,872** (€26,400 without discount) | **€21,834 + freight + storage** | **€22,310 + freight + storage** | |\n\nBefore freight and storage, B is €4,038 cheaper than A and C is €3,562 cheaper than A (with the discount taken). Freight is the deciding line. B only beats A if your freight plus storage from Poznań stays under €4,038 a year. C only beats A if your freight plus storage from Brno stays under €3,562.\n\n**Terms that can change the price or the order:**\n- **C, paper surcharge (C:22–24):** if the paper index rises, C adds 60% of the goods value times the percentage rise, and the discount doesn't apply to it. With zero freight, a rise of about 25.8% would already wipe out C's advantage over A. Every euro of freight and storage lowers that threshold.\n- **A, price fixed until 31.12.2027 (A:26):** A's price can't change, so A's total is the only firm one. Its €0.62 price needs 60,000 boxes a year, so I didn't use it.\n- **B, no price guarantee for the term:** the offer is only valid until 30.11.2026 (B:19), and it doesn't say whether the price holds through 2027.\n- **C, valid only until about 15.11.2026** (30 days from 16.10, C:20). That's less than three weeks from today.\n- **Discount:** without the discount, B and C get relatively cheaper against A (gaps of €4,150 and €3,400). B's lead over C before freight and storage is €476 with the discount and €750 without.\n\n**To finish the comparison I need from you:**\n1. Your freight cost per load from Poznań and from Brno to Nordhessen. For scale: B means two loads of 20,000, C means four loads of 10 pallets each.\n2. Your storage cost per pallet per month.\n3. Whether you usually take the early-payment discount.\n\nWhich offer to accept is your call.",
